questions.stem:
**How many** of the following series are convergent?

$$
\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} (-1)^n \sqrt{n}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{n^3}{n^4 + 5}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{n!}{n^{2002}}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n(\ln n)^2}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \left(1 + \frac{1}{n}\right)^{-n}
$$

**How many** of the following series are **conditionally** convergent?

$$
\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{n\ln n}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{2^n}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n^{0.998}}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=2}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{n}
$$

$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{n^{1.001}}
$$
